//cheflolaskitchen.com/shrimp-stir-fry/"}},"blog-themeatmen-sg-recipes-raindrop-cake":{"url":"https://themeatmen.sg/recipes/raindrop-cake/","author":"","ingredients":[{"name":"Adjust Servings","amount":"","note":""},{"name":"US / Metric","amount":"","note":""},{"name":"MetricUS Customary","amount":"","note":""},{"name":"ml","amount":"","note":""},{"name":"ml","amount":"","note":""},{"name":"Nutriwell snow pear & red date","amount":"","note":""},{"name":"ml","amount":"","note":""},{"name":"ml","amount":"","note":""},{"name":"Nutriwell snow pear & red date","amount":"","note":""},{"name":"g","amount":"","note":""},{"name":"g","amount":"","note":""},{"name":"instant jelly powder","amount":"","note":""},{"name":"g","amount":"","note":""},{"name":"g","amount":"","note":""},{"name":"instant jelly powder","amount":"","note":""},{"name":"pears","amount":"","note":""},{"name":"pears","amount":"","note":""},{"name":"pears","amount":"","note":""},{"name":"pears","amount":"","note":""},{"name":"Ice ball mould","amount":"","note":""},{"name":"Ice ball mould","amount":"","note":""}],"steps":["Heat 500ml Nutriwell snow pear & red date in a pot.","Heat 500ml Nutriwell snow pear & red date in a pot.","Mark as completed"],"tables":[{"title":"Snow Pear and Red Dates Raindrop Cake","preamble":[],"roots":[{"kind":"op","label":"finish","detail":"Mark as completed","inputs":[{"kind":"op","label":"heat","detail":"Heat 500ml Nutriwell snow pear & red date in a pot.","inputs":[{"kind":"op","label":"heat","detail":"Heat 500ml Nutriwell snow pear & red date in a pot.","inputs":[{"kind":"ing","name":"ml","amount":"","note":""},{"kind":"ing","name":"ml","amount":"","note":""},{"kind":"ing","name":"Nutriwell snow pear & red date","amount":"","note":""},{"kind":"ing","name":"ml","amount":"","note":""},{"kind":"ing","name":"ml","amount":"","note":""},{"kind":"ing","name":"Nutriwell snow pear & red date","amount":"","note":""},{"kind":"ing","name":"pears","amount":"","note":""},{"kind":"ing","name":"pears","amount":"","note":""},{"kind":"ing","name":"pears","amount":"","note":""},{"kind":"ing","name":"pears","amount":"","note":""}]}]},{"kind":"ing","name":"Adjust Servings","amount":"","note":"","unplaced":true},{"kind":"ing","name":"US / Metric","amount":"","note":"","unplaced":true},{"kind":"ing","name":"MetricUS Customary","amount":"","note":"","unplaced":true},{"kind":"ing","name":"g","amount":"","note":"","unplaced":true},{"kind":"ing","name":"g","amount":"","note":"","unplaced":true},{"kind":"ing","name":"instant jelly powder","amount":"","note":"","unplaced":true},{"kind":"ing","name":"g","amount":"","note":"","unplaced":true},{"kind":"ing","name":"g","amount":"","note":"","unplaced":true},{"kind":"ing","name":"instant jelly powder","amount":"","note":"","unplaced":true},{"kind":"ing","name":"Ice ball mould","amount":"","note":"","unplaced":true},{"kind":"ing","name":"Ice ball mould","amount":"","note":"","unplaced":true}]}],"post":[],"origin":"generated"}],"photo":"assets/photos/blog-themeatmen-sg-recipes-raindrop-cake.webp","photoCredit":{"from":"own","source":"themeatmen.sg","link":"https://themeatmen.sg/recipes/raindrop-cake/"}},"blog-justonecookbook-com-somen-noodle-soup":{"url":"https://www.justonecookbook.com/somen-noodle-soup/","author":"","ingredients":[{"name":"dashi","amount":"3 cups","note":"Japanese soup stock"},{"name":"soy sauce","amount":"2 Tbsp","note":""},{"name":"mirin","amount":"1½ Tbsp","note":""},{"name":"sugar","amount":"1 tsp","note":""},{"name":"Diamond Crystal kosher salt","amount":"¼ tsp","note":"use half the amount or the same weight for table salt"},{"name":"Shanghai bok choy ((2 oz","amount":"1 head","note":"60 g))"},{"name":"carrot ((1 oz","amount":"2 inches","note":"30 g))"},{"name":"shiitake mushrooms ((1 oz","amount":"4","note":"30 g))"},{"name":"kamaboko","amount":"4 slices","note":"fish cake"},{"name":"eggs","amount":"3 large","note":"50 g each w/o shell"},{"name":"bundles dried somen noodles ((5.3 oz","amount":"3","note":"150 g))"},{"name":"green onion/scallion","amount":"1","note":""},{"name":"mitsuba","amount":"3 sprigs","note":"Japanese parsley"},{"name":"toasted white sesame seeds","amount":"½ tsp","note":""},{"name":"mentsuyu","amount":"6 Tbsp","note":"concentrated noodle soup base"},{"name":"water","amount":"2⅔ cups","note":""},{"name":"mirin","amount":"2 Tbsp","note":""}],"steps":["Gather all the ingredients. For cooking the dried somen noodles, bring a big pot of water to a boil, covered, over medium heat. Once boiling, reduce the heat to low and keep simmering.","In a large pot or donabe (I used this Hario‘s Yukihira Stainless Steel Pot), add 3 cups water and 2 dashi packets. Bring it to a boil, covered, over medium heat. If you have mentsuyu (concentrated noodle soup base), see the instructions below for how to prepare a quick somen broth.","Once boiling, reduce the heat to low and cook, covered, for 2–3 minutes. Then, squeeze the liquid from the dashi packets and discard them.","Add 2 Tbsp soy sauce, 1½ Tbsp mirin, 1 tsp sugar, and ¼ tsp Diamond Crystal kosher salt (use half the amount or the same weight for table salt) and mix it all together. Turn off the heat. Cover the pot with the lid (so the broth doesn’t evaporate) and set it aside.","With a knife, cut 1 head Shanghai bok choy in half lengthwise. Then, cut it into 2-inch (5-cm) pieces. Separate the tough white parts and leafy green parts into two groups and set them aside.","With a vegetable peeler, peel 2 inches carrot and cut it into thin rounds with the knife. Set them aside with the tough white parts of the bok choy.","Remove and discard the stems of 4 shiitake mushrooms. If you‘d like, create a decorative flower cut on the caps called shiitake hanagiri. Set them aside with the leafy green parts of the bok choy.","Detach the bottom of the kamaboko (fish cake) by inserting the knife between the wooden board and fish cake. Then, thinly cut into 4 slices kamaboko (fish cake). Set aside with the leafy vegetables.","Cut 3 sprigs mitsuba (Japanese parsley) and 1 green onion/scallion into small pieces. Set them aside on a small bowl or plate to serve with the soup later on.","In a small bowl, beat 3 large eggs (50 g each w/o shell) with a whisk (I use a flat whisk that I love) and set aside.","Remove the ribbons that wrap around the 3 bundles dried somen noodles. The noodles take only 90 seconds to cook; therefore, you want to start cooking the noodles all at once.","Add the tough white parts of the bok choy and carrots to the simmering broth. Cook, covered, for 4–5 minutes over medium heat.","Add the shiitake mushrooms, kamaboko, and leafy green parts of the bok choy to the broth. Cook, covered, for 2 minutes. During this time, cook the somen noodles (instructions in the next section).","After cooking for 2 minutes, take out the kamaboko and shiitake mushrooms. This is an optional step and only applies if you want to decorate your final dish with kamaboko and shiitake on top of the noodles.","Slowly drizzle a small amount of the beaten eggs over the simmering broth, which will create a fluffy texture. Place your cooking chopsticks at the edge of the bowl that contains the beaten eggs. This will help drizzle the eggs.","Add the cooked somen noodles and let them warm up while the eggs continue to cook.","Place the kamaboko and shiitake mushrooms on top of the noodles. Sprinkle the green onions, mitsuba, and ½ tsp toasted white sesame seeds on top.","Serve the noodles and broth into individual bowls and enjoy!","Add the dried somen noodles to boiling water. Cook according to the package instructions (usually 1½–2 minutes; mine is 1½ minutes). I undercook the noodles by 30 seconds (so I cook the noodles for 60 seconds), since the noodles continue to cook once I place them in the hot broth.","Stir the noodles occasionally, making sure they do not stick to the bottom or the sides of the pot. After cooking, drain the noodles into a sieve.","Rinse the noodles in cold running water until they are cool enough to handle. Then, rinse them as if you are washing your clothes. You need to knead/massage the noodles to get rid of the oil. When you have finished, drain well.","Follow your mentsuyu bottle instructions to make the broth. Your total volume of the broth should be approximately 750 ml or a little more than 3 cups. For my bottle of concentrated mentsuyu, I combine 2⅔ cups water, 6 Tbsp mentsuyu (concentrated noodle soup base), and 2 Tbsp mirin in a large pot. Bring it to a simmer over medium heat. Once simmering, cover with a lid. The somen broth is ready to use.","Refrigerate the noodles, toppings, and broth separately for up to 2–3 days. Reheat in a pot on the stovetop until hot."],"tables":[{"title":"Somen Noodle Soup (Nyumen)","preamble":[],"roots":[{"kind":"op","label":"refrigerate, reheat","detail":"Refrigerate the noodles, toppings, and broth separately for up to 2–3 days. Reheat in a pot on the stovetop until hot.","inputs":[{"kind":"op","label":"finish, combine, heat med heat, simmer","detail":"Follow your mentsuyu bottle instructions to make the broth. Your total volume of the broth should be approximately 750 ml or a little more than 3 cups. For my bottle of concentrated mentsuyu, I combine 2⅔ cups water, 6 Tbsp mentsuyu (concentrated noodle soup base), and 2 Tbsp mirin in a large pot. Bring it to a simmer over medium heat. Once simmering, cover with a lid. The somen broth is ready to use.","inputs":[{"kind":"op","label":"knead, drain","detail":"You need to knead/massage the noodles to get rid of the oil. When you have finished, drain well.","inputs":[{"kind":"ing","name":"oil","amount":"","note":"","implicit":true}]},{"kind":"op","label":"boil, cook 2 min, cook 30 sec, stir, drain, rinse, cool","detail":"Add the dried somen noodles to boiling water. Cook according to the package instructions (usually 1½–2 minutes; mine is 1½ minutes). I undercook the noodles by 30 seconds (so I cook the noodles for 60 seconds), since the noodles continue to cook once I place them in the hot broth. Stir the noodles occasionally, making sure they do not stick to the bottom or the sides of the pot. After cooking, drain the noodles into a sieve. Rinse the noodles in cold running water until they are cool enough to handle. Then, rinse them as if you are washing your clothes.","inputs":[{"kind":"op","label":"serve","detail":"Serve the noodles and broth into individual bowls and enjoy!","inputs":[{"kind":"op","label":"sprinkle, top","detail":"Sprinkle the green onions, mitsuba, and ½ tsp toasted white sesame seeds on top.","inputs":[{"kind":"op","label":"cut, plate, serve","detail":"Cut 3 sprigs mitsuba (Japanese parsley) and 1 green onion/scallion into small pieces. Set them aside on a small bowl or plate to serve with the soup later on.","inputs":[{"kind":"ing","name":"green onion/scallion","amount":"1","note":""},{"kind":"ing","name":"mitsuba","amount":"3 sprigs","note":"Japanese parsley"}]},{"kind":"ing","name":"toasted white sesame seeds","amount":"½ tsp","note":""}]}]},{"kind":"op","label":"drizzle, place, warm, top","detail":"Slowly drizzle a small amount of the beaten eggs over the simmering broth, which will create a fluffy texture. Place your cooking chopsticks at the edge of the bowl that contains the beaten eggs. This will help drizzle the eggs. Add the cooked somen noodles and let them warm up while the eggs continue to cook. Place the kamaboko and shiitake mushrooms on top of the noodles.","inputs":[{"kind":"op","label":"add, cook 2 min, cook, cook 2 min, top","detail":"Add the shiitake mushrooms, kamaboko, and leafy green parts of the bok choy to the broth. Cook, covered, for 2 minutes. During this time, cook the somen noodles (instructions in the next section). After cooking for 2 minutes, take out the kamaboko and shiitake mushrooms. This is an optional step and only applies if you want to decorate your final dish with kamaboko and shiitake on top of the noodles.","inputs":[{"kind":"op","label":"finish, cut, rest","detail":"Detach the bottom of the kamaboko (fish cake) by inserting the knife between the wooden board and fish cake. Then, thinly cut into 4 slices kamaboko (fish cake). Set aside with the leafy vegetables.","inputs":[{"kind":"ing","name":"kamaboko","amount":"4 slices","note":"fish cake"}]},{"kind":"op","label":"add, cook med heat 4–5 min","detail":"Add the tough white parts of the bok choy and carrots to the simmering broth. Cook, covered, for 4–5 minutes over medium heat.","inputs":[{"kind":"op","label":"mix, turn, cover, remove, cook 90 sec","detail":"Add 2 Tbsp soy sauce, 1½ Tbsp mirin, 1 tsp sugar, and ¼ tsp Diamond Crystal kosher salt (use half the amount or the same weight for table salt) and mix it all together. Turn off the heat. Cover the pot with the lid (so the broth doesn’t evaporate) and set it aside. Remove the ribbons that wrap around the 3 bundles dried somen noodles. The noodles take only 90 seconds to cook; therefore, you want to start cooking the noodles all at once.","inputs":[{"kind":"op","label":"squeeze","detail":"Then, squeeze the liquid from the dashi packets and discard them.","inputs":[{"kind":"op","label":"finish, boil, reduce 2–3 min","detail":"If you have mentsuyu (concentrated noodle soup base), see the instructions below for how to prepare a quick somen broth. Once boiling, reduce the heat to low and cook, covered, for 2–3 minutes.","inputs":[{"kind":"ing","name":"mentsuyu","amount":"6 Tbsp","note":"concentrated noodle soup base"}]},{"kind":"op","label":"add, heat med heat","detail":"In a large pot or donabe (I used this Hario‘s Yukihira Stainless Steel Pot), add 3 cups water and 2 dashi packets. Bring it to a boil, covered, over medium heat.","inputs":[{"kind":"ing","name":"dashi","amount":"3 cups","note":"Japanese soup stock"},{"kind":"op","label":"cook med heat, boil, simmer","detail":"Gather all the ingredients. For cooking the dried somen noodles, bring a big pot of water to a boil, covered, over medium heat. Once boiling, reduce the heat to low and keep simmering.","inputs":[{"kind":"ing","name":"water","amount":"2⅔ cups","note":""},{"kind":"ing","name":"bundles dried somen noodles ((5.3 oz","amount":"3","note":"150 g))"}]}]}]},{"kind":"ing","name":"soy sauce","amount":"2 Tbsp","note":""},{"kind":"ing","name":"mirin","amount":"1½ Tbsp","note":""},{"kind":"ing","name":"sugar","amount":"1 tsp","note":""},{"kind":"ing","name":"Diamond Crystal kosher salt","amount":"¼ tsp","note":"use half the amount or the same weight for table salt"},{"kind":"ing","name":"mirin","amount":"2 Tbsp","note":""}]},{"kind":"op","label":"finish","detail":"Set them aside with the leafy green parts of the bok choy.","inputs":[{"kind":"op","label":"remove, cut","detail":"Remove and discard the stems of 4 shiitake mushrooms. If you‘d like, create a decorative flower cut on the caps called shiitake hanagiri.","inputs":[{"kind":"ing","name":"shiitake mushrooms ((1 oz","amount":"4","note":"30 g))"}]},{"kind":"op","label":"peel, cut","detail":"With a vegetable peeler, peel 2 inches carrot and cut it into thin rounds with the knife. Set them aside with the tough white parts of the bok choy.","inputs":[{"kind":"op","label":"cut","detail":"With a knife, cut 1 head Shanghai bok choy in half lengthwise. Then, cut it into 2-inch (5-cm) pieces. Separate the tough white parts and leafy green parts into two groups and set them aside.","inputs":[{"kind":"ing","name":"Shanghai bok choy ((2 oz","amount":"1 head","note":"60 g))"}]},{"kind":"ing","name":"carrot ((1 oz","amount":"2 inches","note":"30 g))"}]}]}]}]},{"kind":"op","label":"beat, whisk","detail":"In a small bowl, beat 3 large eggs (50 g each w/o shell) with a whisk (I use a flat whisk that I love) and set aside.","inputs":[{"kind":"ing","name":"eggs","amount":"3 large","note":"50 g each w/o shell"}]}]}]}]}]}],"post":[],"origin":"generated"}],"photo":"assets/photos/blog-justonecookbook-com-somen-noodle-soup.webp","photoCredit":{"from":"own","source":"justonecookbook.com","link":"https://www.justonecookbook.com/somen-noodle-soup/"}},"mealdb-52992":{"url":"https://www.themealdb.com/meal/52992","ingredients":[{"name":"Potatoes","amount":"5"},{"name":"Carrots","amount":"12 ounces"},{"name":"Scallions","amount":"1"},{"name":"Garlic","amount":"2 cloves"},{"name":"Bread","amount":"1 Slice"},{"name":"Garlic Powder","amount":"1"},{"name":"Soy Sauce","amount":"2"},{"name":"Ground Beef","amount":"1"},{"name":"Vegetable Oil","amount":"1 tsp"},{"name":"Sugar","amount":"2 tsp"},{"name":"Butter","amount":"2 tbsp"}],"steps":["Preheat oven to 425 degrees. Wash and dry all produce. Dice potatoes into 1/2-inch pieces. Trim, peel, and cut carrots on a diagonal into 1/2-inch-thick pieces. Trim and thinly slice scallions, separating whites from greens; finely chop whites. Peel and finely chop garlic.","In a medium bowl, soak bread with 2 TBSP water (4 TBSP for 4 servings); break up with your hands until pasty. Stir in beef, sriracha, scallion whites, half the garlic, salt (we used 3/4 tsp kosher salt; 11/2 tsp for 4), and pepper. Form into two 1-inch-tall loaves (four loaves for 4). Place on one side of a baking sheet. Toss carrots on empty side of same sheet with a drizzle of oil, salt, and pepper. (For 4, spread meatloaves out across whole sheet and add carrots to a second sheet.) Bake for 20 minutes (we'll glaze the meatloaves then).","Meanwhile, place potatoes in a medium pot with enough salted water to cover by 2 inches. Bring to a boil and cook until very","tender, 12-15 minutes. Reserve 1/2 cup potato cooking liquid, then drain. While potatoes cook, in a small bowl, combine soy sauce, garlic powder, 1/4 cup ketchup (1/2 cup for 4 servings), and 2 tsp sugar (4 tsp for 4).","Once meatloaves and carrots have baked 20 minutes, remove from oven. Spoon half the ketchup glaze over meatloaves (save","the rest for serving); return to oven until carrots are browned and tender, meatloaves are cooked through, and glaze is tacky, 4-5 minutes more.","Meanwhile, melt 2 TBSP butter (4 TBSP for 4 servings) in pot used for potatoes over medium heat. Add remaining garlic and cook","until fragrant, 30 seconds. Add potatoes and 1/4 tsp wasabi. Mash, adding splashes of reserved potato cooking liquid as necessary until smooth. Season with salt and pepper. (If you like things spicy, stir in more wasabi!)","Divide meatloaves, mashed potatoes, and roasted carrots between plates. Sprinkle with scallion greens and serve with remaining ketchup glaze on the side for dipping."],"tables":[{"title":"Soy-Glazed Meatloaves with Wasabi Mashed Potatoes and Roasted Carrots","preamble":["Preheat oven to 425 degrees."],"roots":[{"kind":"op","label":"divide, roast, sprinkle, glaze","detail":"Divide meatloaves, mashed potatoes, and roasted carrots between plates. Sprinkle with scallion greens and serve with remaining ketchup glaze on the side for dipping.","inputs":[{"kind":"op","label":"30 sec, add, mash, season, stir in","detail":"until fragrant, 30 seconds. Add potatoes and 1/4 tsp wasabi. Mash, adding splashes of reserved potato cooking liquid as necessary until smooth. Season with salt and pepper. (If you like things spicy, stir in more wasabi!)","inputs":[{"kind":"op","label":"melt med heat, add","detail":"Meanwhile, melt 2 TBSP butter (4 TBSP for 4 servings) in pot used for potatoes over medium heat. Add remaining garlic and cook","inputs":[{"kind":"op","label":"brown, glaze 4–5 min","detail":"the rest for serving); return to oven until carrots are browned and tender, meatloaves are cooked through, and glaze is tacky, 4-5 minutes more.","inputs":[{"kind":"op","label":"combine, bake 20 min, glaze","detail":"While potatoes cook, in a small bowl, combine soy sauce, garlic powder, 1/4 cup ketchup (1/2 cup for 4 servings), and 2 tsp sugar (4 tsp for 4). Once meatloaves and carrots have baked 20 minutes, remove from oven. Spoon half the ketchup glaze over meatloaves (save","inputs":[{"kind":"op","label":"12–15 min, drain","detail":"tender, 12-15 minutes. Reserve 1/2 cup potato cooking liquid, then drain.","inputs":[{"kind":"op","label":"place, boil","detail":"Meanwhile, place potatoes in a medium pot with enough salted water to cover by 2 inches. Bring to a boil and cook until very","inputs":[{"kind":"op","label":"wash, dry, dice","detail":"Wash and dry all produce. Dice potatoes into 1/2-inch pieces.","inputs":[{"kind":"ing","name":"Potatoes","amount":"5","note":""}]},{"kind":"op","label":"toss, spread, bake 20 min","detail":"Toss carrots on empty side of same sheet with a drizzle of oil, salt, and pepper. (For 4, spread meatloaves out across whole sheet and add carrots to a second sheet.) Bake for 20 minutes (we'll glaze the meatloaves then).","inputs":[{"kind":"op","label":"trim, cut","detail":"Trim, peel, and cut carrots on a diagonal into 1/2-inch-thick pieces.","inputs":[{"kind":"ing","name":"Carrots","amount":"12 ounces","note":""}]},{"kind":"op","label":"stir in, form, place","detail":"Stir in beef, sriracha, scallion whites, half the garlic, salt (we used 3/4 tsp kosher salt; 11/2 tsp for 4), and pepper. Form into two 1-inch-tall loaves (four loaves for 4). Place on one side of a baking sheet.","inputs":[{"kind":"op","label":"soak, bread","detail":"In a medium bowl, soak bread with 2 TBSP water (4 TBSP for 4 servings); break up with your hands until pasty.","inputs":[{"kind":"ing","name":"Bread","amount":"1 Slice","note":""},{"kind":"ing","name":"water","amount":"2 TBSP","note":"","implicit":true}]},{"kind":"op","label":"trim, chop","detail":"Trim and thinly slice scallions, separating whites from greens; finely chop whites.","inputs":[{"kind":"ing","name":"Scallions","amount":"1","note":""}]},{"kind":"op","label":"peel, chop","detail":"Peel and finely chop garlic.","inputs":[{"kind":"ing","name":"Garlic","amount":"2 cloves","note":""}]},{"kind":"ing","name":"Ground Beef","amount":"1","note":""},{"kind":"ing","name":"kosher salt","amount":"3/4 tsp","note":"","implicit":true},{"kind":"ing","name":"pepper","amount":"","note":"","implicit":true},{"kind":"ing","name":"salt","amount":"","note":"","implicit":true}]},{"kind":"ing","name":"Vegetable Oil","amount":"1 tsp","note":""}]}]}]},{"kind":"ing","name":"Garlic Powder","amount":"1","note":""},{"kind":"ing","name":"Soy Sauce","amount":"2","note":""},{"kind":"ing","name":"Sugar","amount":"2 tsp","note":""}]}]},{"kind":"ing","name":"Butter","amount":"2 tbsp","note":""}]}]}]}],"post":[],"origin":"generated"}],"photo":"assets/photos/mealdb-52992.webp","photoCredit":{"from":"own","source":"TheMealDB","link":"https://www.themealdb.com/meal/52992"}},"blog-recipetineats-com-spaghetti-alla-puttanesca":{"url":"https://www.recipetineats.com/spaghetti-alla-puttanesca/","author":"","ingredients":[{"name":"/ 7oz spaghetti","amount":"200 g","note":", or other long pasta"},{"name":"extra virgin olive oil","amount":"2 tbsp","note":", plus more for drizzling"},{"name":"garlic cloves (","amount":"2","note":"finely minced (knife, not garlic press))"},{"name":"anchovy fillets (","amount":"3","note":"finely minced (Note 1))"},{"name":"pitted black olives (","amount":"1/4 cup","note":"preferably in oil, quartered (Note 2))"},{"name":"capers (","amount":"1 tbsp","note":"drained (Note 3))"},{"name":"chilli flakes ((red pepper flakes))","amount":"1/4 tsp","note":""},{"name":"water","amount":"1/2 cup","note":""},{"name":"fresh oregano (","amount":"1 tsp","note":"roughly chopped (sub 1/4 tsp dried))"},{"name":"kosher / cooking salt ((or 2 pinches table salt))","amount":"1/8 tsp","note":""},{"name":"black pepper","amount":"1/8 tsp","note":""},{"name":"sugar (","amount":"1/4 tsp","note":"if needed (depends on tomato quality, Note 4))"},{"name":"fresh basil (","amount":"2 tbsp","note":"roughly chopped (Note 6))"}],"steps":["Prepare: Bring a large pot of water to the boil, ready for the pasta. Warm serving bowls (I microwave 1 minute).","Cook garlic: Heat olive oil in a medium skillet over medium high heat. Add garlic and cook for 15 seconds until it starts turning golden.","Cook anchovies: Add anchovies, capers, olives and chilli flakes. Cook for 1 minute.","Tomato: Add tomato, then add the 1/2 cup of water into the can. Swirl around to rinse then pour into the skillet.","Simmer: Add oregano, salt and pepper. Stir, bring to simmer, then turn down to low and cook over medium heat for 10 minutes or until the tomato has broken down and created a sauce. Turn off stove when ready if not timed with cooked pasta.","Cook pasta: Meanwhile, add 2 teaspoons salt into the pot of water. Then add pasta and cook per packet directions.","Reserve pasta water (Note 5): Just before draining, scoop out a mugful of pasta cooking water and set aside. Then drain pasta in a colander.","Toss pasta: Immediately add pasta into sauce. Add 1/4 cup of pasta cooking water reserved from previous step (Note 5) then use 2 wooden spoons to toss the pasta, still on a low stove, for 1 minute or until the sauce is no longer in the skillet but rather clinging to the pasta strands (but still slick and slippery). If the pasta gets too dry, add more pasta cooking water and toss.","Serve: Immediately transfer into warmed bowls. Drizzle with olive oil, sprinkle with basil. Serve immediately!"],"tables":[{"title":"Spaghetti alla Puttanesca","preamble":[],"roots":[{"kind":"op","label":"drizzle, sprinkle, serve","detail":"Drizzle with olive oil, sprinkle with basil. Serve immediately!","inputs":[{"kind":"ing","name":"fresh basil (","amount":"2 tbsp","note":"roughly chopped (Note 6))"},{"kind":"op","label":"serve","detail":"Serve: Immediately transfer into warmed bowls.","inputs":[{"kind":"op","label":"toss, dry, toss","detail":"Toss pasta: Immediately add pasta into sauce. Add 1/4 cup of pasta cooking water reserved from previous step (Note 5) then use 2 wooden spoons to toss the pasta, still on a low stove, for 1 minute or until the sauce is no longer in the skillet but rather clinging to the pasta strands (but still slick and slippery). If the pasta gets too dry, add more pasta cooking water and toss.","inputs":[{"kind":"op","label":"drain","detail":"Reserve pasta water (Note 5): Just before draining, scoop out a mugful of pasta cooking water and set aside. Then drain pasta in a colander.","inputs":[{"kind":"op","label":"cook, add","detail":"Cook pasta: Meanwhile, add 2 teaspoons salt into the pot of water. Then add pasta and cook per packet directions.","inputs":[{"kind":"op","label":"simmer, turn","detail":"Simmer: Add oregano, salt and pepper. Stir, bring to simmer, then turn down to low and cook over medium heat for 10 minutes or until the tomato has broken down and created a sauce. Turn off stove when ready if not timed with cooked pasta.","inputs":[{"kind":"op","label":"add, rinse","detail":"Tomato: Add tomato, then add the 1/2 cup of water into the can. Swirl around to rinse then pour into the skillet.","inputs":[{"kind":"op","label":"cook","detail":"Cook anchovies: Add anchovies, capers, olives and chilli flakes. Cook for 1 minute.","inputs":[{"kind":"op","label":"cook med-high heat, add 15 sec","detail":"Cook garlic: Heat olive oil in a medium skillet over medium high heat. Add garlic and cook for 15 seconds until it starts turning golden.","inputs":[{"kind":"ing","name":"garlic cloves (","amount":"2","note":"finely minced (knife, not garlic press))"},{"kind":"ing","name":"extra virgin olive oil","amount":"2 tbsp","note":", plus more for drizzling"}]},{"kind":"ing","name":"capers (","amount":"1 tbsp","note":"drained (Note 3))"},{"kind":"ing","name":"chilli flakes ((red pepper flakes))","amount":"1/4 tsp","note":""},{"kind":"ing","name":"anchovy fillets (","amount":"3","note":"finely minced (Note 1))"},{"kind":"ing","name":"pitted black olives (","amount":"1/4 cup","note":"preferably in oil, quartered (Note 2))"}]},{"kind":"op","label":"finish, warm 1 min","detail":"Prepare: Bring a large pot of water to the boil, ready for the pasta. Warm serving bowls (I microwave 1 minute).","inputs":[{"kind":"ing","name":"water","amount":"1/2 cup","note":""}]}]},{"kind":"ing","name":"fresh oregano (","amount":"1 tsp","note":"roughly chopped (sub 1/4 tsp dried))"},{"kind":"ing","name":"kosher / cooking salt ((or 2 pinches table salt))","amount":"1/8 tsp","note":""},{"kind":"ing","name":"black pepper","amount":"1/8 tsp","note":""}]}]}]}]}]},{"kind":"ing","name":"/ 7oz spaghetti","amount":"200 g","note":", or other long pasta","unplaced":true},{"kind":"ing","name":"sugar (","amount":"1/4 tsp","note":"if needed (depends on tomato quality, Note 4))","unplaced":true}]}],"post":[],"origin":"generated"}],"photo":"assets/photos/blog-recipetineats-com-spaghetti-alla-puttanesca.webp","photoCredit":{"from":"own","source":"recipetineats.com","link":"https://www.recipetineats.com/spaghetti-alla-puttanesca/"}},"blog-nzwomansweeklyfood-co-nz-uick-and-easy-spiced-lamb-cutlets-with-crispy-chickpeas-8626":{"url":"https://www.nzwomansweeklyfood.co.nz/recipe/quick-and-easy/spiced-lamb-cutlets-with-crispy-chickpeas-8626/","author":"Nici Wickes","ingredients":[{"name":"chickpeas","amount":"400 gram can","note":"drained"},{"name":"paprika","amount":"1 teaspoon","note":""},{"name":"olive oil","amount":"3 tablespoon","note":""},{"name":"each of fennel seeds","amount":"1 teaspoon","note":"ground coriander, ground cumin, turmeric"},{"name":"thick-cut lamb cutlets","amount":"8","note":"or use lamb loin chops"},{"name":"cherry tomatoes","amount":"1 cup","note":""},{"name":"handful of baby spinach leaves","amount":"","note":""},{"name":"sea salt","amount":"1 teaspoon","note":""},{"name":"plain yoghurt","amount":"1/2 cup","note":""},{"name":"juice of 1/2 a lemon","amount":"","note":""},{"name":"small handful each of mint and coriander","amount":"","note":""}],"steps":["Toss the drained chickpeas in paprika and 2 tablespoons of the olive oil and roast for 15-20 minutes at 180°C or until crispy. Set aside.","Mix the spices together. Heat your BBQ grill to medium-high and brush one side of the lamb cutlets with the remaining olive oil. Place on your grill, oiled side down, and cook until dark grill marks appear, then flip. Sprinkle more of the spices over the cooked side and continue cooking until any fat is rendered (it goes from white to clear) and the meat is medium-rare. This will depend on the thickness of your lamb of course, and regular checking by pressing the meat to ensure it still has some 'give' in it is important.Remove from the grill, sprinkle over more of spice mix and leave to rest. The spices will meld nicely into the meat and will be warmed through to release their flavours.","Next, blister the tomatoes on the BBQ grill or a hot plate.","To serve: Scatter the spinach on a large serving plate. Add the chickpeas, tomatoes and your lamb and season it all with salt. Mix the yoghurt and lemon juice together, spoon this over and then scatter over the fresh herbs. Serve extra yoghurt dressing on the side."],"tables":[{"title":"Spiced Lamb Cutlets with Crispy Chickpeas","preamble":[],"roots":[{"kind":"op","label":"mix, juice, serve","detail":"Mix the yoghurt and lemon juice together, spoon this over and then scatter over the fresh herbs. Serve extra yoghurt dressing on the side.","inputs":[{"kind":"ing","name":"lemon juice","amount":"","note":"","implicit":true},{"kind":"ing","name":"plain yoghurt","amount":"1/2 cup","note":""},{"kind":"ing","name":"juice of 1/2 a lemon","amount":"","note":""},{"kind":"op","label":"add","detail":"Add the chickpeas, tomatoes and your lamb and season it all with salt.","inputs":[{"kind":"op","label":"serve, plate","detail":"To serve: Scatter the spinach on a large serving plate.","inputs":[{"kind":"ing","name":"handful of baby spinach leaves","amount":"","note":""}]},{"kind":"op","label":"grill, brush, sprinkle, sprinkle, mix, warm","detail":"Heat your BBQ grill to medium-high and brush one side of the lamb cutlets with the remaining olive oil. Place on your grill, oiled side down, and cook until dark grill marks appear, then flip. Sprinkle more of the spices over the cooked side and continue cooking until any fat is rendered (it goes from white to clear) and the meat is medium-rare. This will depend on the thickness of your lamb of course, and regular checking by pressing the meat to ensure it still has some 'give' in it is important.Remove from the grill, sprinkle over more of spice mix and leave to rest. The spices will meld nicely into the meat and will be warmed through to release their flavours.","inputs":[{"kind":"op","label":"toss, roast 180°C 15–20 min, rest","detail":"Toss the drained chickpeas in paprika and 2 tablespoons of the olive oil and roast for 15-20 minutes at 180°C or until crispy. Set aside.","inputs":[{"kind":"ing","name":"chickpeas","amount":"400 gram can","note":"drained"},{"kind":"ing","name":"paprika","amount":"1 teaspoon","note":""},{"kind":"ing","name":"olive oil","amount":"3 tablespoon","note":""}]},{"kind":"ing","name":"thick-cut lamb cutlets","amount":"8","note":"or use lamb loin chops"}]},{"kind":"op","label":"grill, plate","detail":"Next, blister the tomatoes on the BBQ grill or a hot plate.","inputs":[{"kind":"ing","name":"cherry tomatoes","amount":"1 cup","note":""}]},{"kind":"ing","name":"sea salt","amount":"1 teaspoon","note":""}]},{"kind":"op","label":"mix","detail":"Mix the spices together.","inputs":[{"kind":"ing","name":"each of fennel seeds","amount":"1 teaspoon","note":"ground coriander, ground cumin, turmeric"},{"kind":"ing","name":"small handful each of mint and coriander","amount":"","note":""}]}]}],"post":[],"origin":"generated"}],"photo":"assets/photos/blog-nzwomansweeklyfood-co-nz-uick-and-easy-spiced-lamb-cutlets-with-crispy-chickpeas-8626.webp","photoCredit":{"from":"own","source":"nzwomansweeklyfood.co.nz","link":"https://www.nzwomansweeklyfood.co.nz/recipe/quick-and-easy/spiced-lamb-cutlets-with-crispy-chickpeas-8626/"}},"blog-globaltableadventure-com-recipe-lamb-brochettes-broasheht":{"url":"https://globaltableadventure.c